# State & Hooks Rules

## When to use what
| Need | Tool |
|------|------|
| Component-local ephemeral state | `useState` / `useReducer` |
| Shared UI/client state | Zustand store |
| Server data | React Query — never copy into Zustand |
| Form state | react-hook-form |

## Zustand rules
- Never store server data in Zustand.
- One store per domain or feature.
- Export a typed interface: `interface FeatureStore { ... }`.
- Subscribe to slices: `useStore(s => s.field)` — never the whole store object.
- Expose a `reset()` action for logout/unmount cleanup.

## React Query rules
- `queryKey` must be fully descriptive: `['users', userId, 'posts']`.
- Set `staleTime` explicitly on every `useQuery` — never rely on the default 0.
- Use `select` to reshape data instead of transforming in the component.
- Invalidate only the minimum necessary keys after mutations.

## Custom hooks
- Live in `src/hooks/` (shared) or `src/features/[name]/hooks/` (scoped).
- Always prefixed with `use`.
- Never call hooks inside conditions, loops, or nested functions.
- One concern per hook.
